  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Virginia has received $1.3B in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Obligations fell 98.9% year over year. Award activity includes 4,082 awards with an average award size of $327K. Year-to-date totals are partial, so the FY2027 figure represents fiscal year to date obligations. Historical context shows much larger annual totals in prior fiscal years: FY26 recorded $118B, FY25 recorded $121B, FY24 recorded $110B, FY23 recorded $106B, and FY22 recorded $89.4B. The Department of Veterans Affairs dominated buying in FY2027 to date with $1.1B in obligations. Other notable buying agencies include the Department of Commerce with $92.8M and the Department of Health and Human Services with $27M. TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP is the largest vendor in FY2027 to date with $900M in obligations. Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers is the largest industry by obligations in FY2027 to date with $900M. The data reflect where federal dollars have flowed in Virginia so far in FY2027; totals may change as the fiscal year progresses.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top buying agencies in Virginia this fiscal year?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $1.1B in FY2027 to date. The Department of Commerce obligated $92.8M and the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $27M. The Department of Homeland Security, General Services Administration, and Department of the Treasury follow with $21.8M, $19.3M, and $12.5M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which vendors and industries received the most obligations in Virginia?",
        "body": "TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP received $900M in FY2027 to date. THUNDERCAT TECHNOLOGY, LLC received $139M and GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. received $60.7M. Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers accounted for $900M and Other Computer Related Services accounted for $225M in industry obligations."
      }
    ]
